   "date": "2015-10-15T17:18:06Z",
   "subject": "Merging two plots of different type with same x-axis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi—I have data on annual tree growth, annual precipitation, and long-term average precipitation from 58 sites. I have estimated the coefficient of the annual growth-precipitation relationship, and for each site, I would like to show two things:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">a) the growth-precipitation coefficient (scatterplot with one dot per site)<br>b) the long-term average precipitation (single-row “heatmap”, or grid plot, with color indicating normal precipitation)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I have produced each of these plots separately in ggplot using the attached data.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">library(ggplot2)\r\n\r\nplots.fits &lt;- read.csv(&quot;plots_fits.csv&quot;,header=TRUE)\r\n\r\n## Order sites (&quot;plots&quot;) (for x-axis) by geographic cluster and then by decreasing long-term average precipitation\r\nplot.levels &lt;- unique(plots.fits$<a href=\"http://plot.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745875000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2miceiAJeWS_NKcWObI-V9\">plot.id</a>[order(plots.fits$cluster,-plots.fits$ppt.normal)])\r\nplots.fits$<a href=\"http://plot.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745875000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2miceiAJeWS_NKcWObI-V9\">plot.id</a> &lt;- factor(plots.fits$<a href=\"http://plot.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745875000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2miceiAJeWS_NKcWObI-V9\">plot.id</a>,levels=plot.levels)\r\n\r\n## first plot (scatterplot)\r\nggplot(plots.fits,aes(x=<a href=\"http://plot.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745875000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2miceiAJeWS_NKcWObI-V9\">plot.id</a>,y=ppt.coef.mean,colour=ppt.normal)) +\r\n  geom_point(aes(size=ppt.r.sq)) +  #make size of point proportional to R-sq of linear model fit\r\n  geom_errorbar(aes(ymin=ppt.coef.mean-ppt.coef.stderr,ymax=ppt.coef.mean+ppt.coef.stderr))+\r\n  facet_grid(. ~ cluster,scales=&quot;free_x&quot;,space=&quot;free_x&quot;) + #plot separate facet for each geographic region, or &quot;cluster&quot;\r\n\r\n## second plot (&quot;heatmap&quot; of long-term average precipitation)\r\nggplot(plots.fits,aes(x=<a href=\"http://plot.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745875000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2miceiAJeWS_NKcWObI-V9\">plot.id</a>,y=1,fill=ppt.normal)) +\r\n  geom_tile(stat=&quot;identity&quot;) +\r\n  facet_grid(. ~ cluster,scales=&quot;free_x&quot;,space=&quot;free_x&quot;)+\r\n  theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 90,hjust=1,vjust=0.5))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"><img style=\"margin-right:0px\" alt=\"Inline image 1\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug/attach/8644ef036e749/image.png?part=0.0.2&amp;view=1\" height=\"177\" width=\"496\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"><img alt=\"Inline image 2\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug/attach/8644ef036e749/image.png?part=0.0.1&amp;view=1\" height=\"75\" width=\"496\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">But what I really want is something like this:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"><img alt=\"Inline image 3\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug/attach/8644ef036e749/image.png?part=0.0.3&amp;view=1\" height=\"206\" width=\"496\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Ugly photoshopping, but you get the idea.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">It this possible in ggplot2 or any other R package(s)?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Thanks!</p><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Derek<br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">—<br>Derek Young, Ph.D. Candidate<br>Graduate Group in Ecology<br>Department of Plant Sciences<br>University of California, Davis<br><a href=\"http://www.changingforests.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.changingforests.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745875000&amp;usg=AOvVaw04ltzLoZisjnDW8NqABMHA\">http://www.changingforests.com</a></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdiBkaXI9Imx0ciI+PGRpdj48ZGl2PjxkaXY+SGktLUkgaGF2ZSBkYXRhIG9uIGFubnVhbCB0\r\ncmVlIGdyb3d0aCwgYW5udWFsIHByZWNpcGl0YXRpb24sIGFuZCBsb25nLXRlcm0gYXZlcmFnZSBw\r\ncmVjaXBpdGF0aW9uIGZyb20gNTggc2l0ZXMuIEkgaGF2ZSBlc3RpbWF0ZWQgdGhlIGNvZWZmaWNp\r\nZW50IG9mIHRoZSBhbm51YWwgZ3Jvd3RoLXByZWNpcGl0YXRpb24gcmVsYXRpb25zaGlwLCBhbmQg\r\nZm9yIGVhY2ggc2l0ZSwgSSB3b3VsZCBsaWtlIHRvIHNob3cgdHdvIHRoaW5nczo8YnI+PGJyPmEp\r\nIHRoZSBncm93dGgtcHJlY2lwaXRhdGlvbiBjb2VmZmljaWVudCAoc2NhdHRlcnBsb3Qgd2l0aCBv\r\nbmUgZG90IHBlciBzaXRlKTxicj48L2Rpdj5iKSB0aGUgbG9uZy10ZXJtIGF2ZXJhZ2UgcHJlY2lw\r\naXRhdGlvbiAoc2luZ2xlLXJvdyAiaGVhdG1hcCIsIG9yIGdyaWQgcGxvdCwgd2l0aCBjb2xvciBp\r\nbmRpY2F0aW5nIG5vcm1hbCBwcmVjaXBpdGF0aW9uKTxicj48YnI+PC9kaXY+SSBoYXZlIHByb2R1\r\nY2VkIGVhY2ggb2YgdGhlc2UgcGxvdHMgc2VwYXJhdGVseSBpbiBnZ3Bsb3QgdXNpbmcgdGhlIGF0\r\ndGFjaGVkIGRhdGEuPGJyPjxicj48L2Rpdj5gYGA8YnI+PGRpdj5saWJyYXJ5KGdncGxvdDIpPGJy\r\nPjxicj5wbG90cy5maXRzICZsdDstIHJlYWQuY3N2KCJwbG90c19maXR