     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"font-family:Times,Arial;font-size:14px;color:rgba(0,0,0,1.0);margin:0px;line-height:auto\">If you want to do it in base R, you could put multiple plots on one figure using <a href=\"http://plot.new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://plot.new&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467745879000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QAJYhZwKrC342m3CLPkSv\">plot.new</a>() and then new = TRUE in the plot function. </div><div style=\"font-family:Times,Arial;font-size:14px;color:rgba(0,0,0,1.0);margin:0px;line-height:auto\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Times,Arial;font-size:14px;color:rgba(0,0,0,1.0);margin:0px;line-height:auto\">CH</div><div style=\"font-family:Times,Arial;font-size:14px;color:rgba(0,0,0,1.0);margin:0px;line-height:auto\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Times,Arial;font-size:14px;color:rgba(0,0,0,1.0);margin:0px;line-height:auto\"><br></div> <div><div style=\"font-family:helvetica,arial;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:normal\">-- </span><br style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"line-height:normal;font-size:14px;font-family:helvetica\">Christopher Hamm<br>Postdoctoral Researcher<br>Department of Ecology and Evolutionary Biology<br>University of Kansas</span><span style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:normal\"></span><div style=\"line-height:normal;font-size:12.727272033691406px;font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">5032 Haworth Hall</span></div><div style=\"line-height:normal;font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">1200 Sunnyside Avenue</span></div><div style=\"line-height:normal;font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lawrence, Kansas 66045-7566</span></div><div style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:normal;font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">USA</span></div><div style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:normal;font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-si